From 3186e8ffda25b1ffc989097aa4361175de3a6d80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:41:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(deburr): chord width, Constant Depth sizing and
 multi-pass breaks

A 3D Deburr `width` is now the chamfer chord w = 2 s sin(theta / 2)
on each wedge angle theta. The setback s and the tip's drop follow
from the edge's own wedge. Constant Depth holds d = s cos(theta / 2).
A break can take 1 to 100 passes, from the outer break in to the
final one; only the final break is declared. A Round profile refuses
by name on the sharp cone.

The project file steps to v75. A v74 Deburr width is multiplied by
sqrt(2), its chord on a 90-degree edge, so the cut depth stays.
The settings ride the command history, the file, MCP and the UI.

Fixes #1890

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
